;; A Java forms program whose system properties are data (A13 of the Ghidra case study's G1 plan; program.edn
;; :properties, j2g --property): set at the start, before any class of the program is initialized, so a class
;; initializer reads them (as a library's switches, java.awt.headless, are read); a value with = and spaces kept
;; whole; a property the JDK sets itself (java.vm.name) left as the runtime has it unless named.
{:main-class props.Main
 :properties {"java.awt.headless" "true"
              "sample.mode" "a=b c"
              "sample.empty" ""}}
